! The kick ring with a collimator that takes 12,000 particles under the 10,000 general thresholds on
! the first pass, and a PFILTER, which the device doesn't take, so the beam goes to the host each pass.
QF: KQUAD,L=0.3,K1=1.2,N_SLICES=16
QD: KQUAD,L=0.3,K1=-1.2,N_SLICES=16
SF: KSEXT,L=0.2,K2=5,N_SLICES=8
D: DRIF,L=0.5
COL: RCOL,X_MAX=2.5e-4
PF: PFILTER,DELTALIMIT=0.5
CELL: LINE=(QF,D,QD,D,SF,D)
! W's sums are the sign of where the beam was: the device adds them in its own order, so they differ
! from the CPU's in the last digits, while the particles come out the same from either side.
W: WATCH,FILENAME="%s.w1",MODE="parameter"
RING: LINE=(COL,4*CELL,W,PF)
